IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgg-scope`
IMPORT `sgg-lodging`

-- Tests for sgg-lodging.l4 (ss 368 to 371). Expected values are written from the text of each subsection, beside the assertion.
-- Dates: Date day month year. A `-- EXPECT` comment above a #TRACE says what the trace must print; the lead checks each against the output.

§ `Section 368(1): what must be lodged`

-- Field order of `s 368(1) lodgment`: (a); (b); (c) the law requires the instrument to be registered or lodged; (c) lodged; (d); (e); (f);
-- (g) notice of the situation lodged; (g) office open and accessible on each business day; (g) days and hours lodged; (h)(i); (h)(ii); (h)(iii);
-- (i) the law requires audited statements of the head office; (i) lodged.
`s 368(1) test everything lodged` MEANS `s 368(1) lodgment` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s 368(1) test nothing lodged and nothing conditional applies` MEANS `s 368(1) lodgment` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 368(1) test only the conditional paragraphs fall away` MEANS `s 368(1) lodgment` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 368(1) test paragraph (c) applies but its instrument is not lodged` MEANS `s 368(1) lodgment` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 368(1) test paragraph (g) hours are not lodged and the office is not always open` MEANS `s 368(1) lodgment` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s 368(1) test paragraph (i) applies but the statements are not lodged` MEANS `s 368(1) lodgment` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 368(1) the foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires` `s 368(1) test everything lodged` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- paragraph (c) "but only if" the law of the place of incorporation requires the instrument to be lodged; paragraph (g) days and hours "unless" always open; paragraph (i) "where" the law requires.
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires` `s 368(1) test only the conditional paragraphs fall away` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires` `s 368(1) test paragraph (c) applies but its instrument is not lodged` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires` `s 368(1) test paragraph (i) applies but the statements are not lodged` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the foreign company has lodged what the subsection requires` `s 368(1) test nothing lodged and nothing conditional applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the paragraphs of the subsection not yet complied with` `s 368(1) test everything lodged` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the paragraphs of the subsection not yet complied with` `s 368(1) test paragraph (c) applies but its instrument is not lodged` EQUALS LIST "(c) a certified copy of the charter, statute, constitution or articles"
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the paragraphs of the subsection not yet complied with` `s 368(1) test paragraph (g) hours are not lodged and the office is not always open` EQUALS LIST "(g) notice of the days and hours the registered office is open"
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the paragraphs of the subsection not yet complied with` `s 368(1) test paragraph (i) applies but the statements are not lodged` EQUALS LIST "(i) a copy of the latest audited financial statements of the head office"
#ASSERT count (`s 368(1) the paragraphs of the subsection not yet complied with` `s 368(1) test nothing lodged and nothing conditional applies`) EQUALS 10

-- "before it establishes a place of business": lodging the day before is before; the same day is not.
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the foreign company lodged the documents before it began` (Date 9 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the foreign company lodged the documents before it began` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the foreign company lodged the documents before it began` (Date 11 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "and on payment of the appropriate fees and subject to this Act, the Registrar must register": lodged, paid, nothing in the Act in the way.
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the Registrar must register the foreign company under this Division` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the Registrar must register the foreign company under this Division` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the Registrar must register the foreign company under this Division` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- another provision of the Act (section 369 or 378) requires or permits refusal: the duty is "subject to this Act": not covered.
#ASSERT `s 368(1) the Registrar must register the foreign company under this Division` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the last permitted day is day 9 (the company begins on day 10).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 368(1) the foreign company must lodge the documents before it establishes a place of business or commences to carry on business` "Overseas Co" 9 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 368(1) lodge with the Registrar for registration the documents the subsection lists` AT 9
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 368(1) the foreign company must lodge the documents before it establishes a place of business or commences to carry on business` "Overseas Co" 9 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 368(1) lodge with the Registrar for registration the documents the subsection lists` AT 10
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 368(1) the foreign company must lodge the documents before it establishes a place of business or commences to carry on business` "Overseas Co" 9 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§ `Section 368(2) to (4)`

-- (2) addressed and left at, or posted to, the residential address OR the contact address.
#ASSERT `s 368(2) the document is sufficiently served on the director or authorised representative` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368(2) the document is sufficiently served on the director or authorised representative` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368(2) the document is sufficiently served on the director or authorised representative` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not addressed to the person: the "if" is unmet.
#ASSERT `s 368(2) the document is sufficiently served on the director or authorised representative` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a document the Act does not require to be served on a director or authorised representative: outside the subsection.
#ASSERT `s 368(2) the document is sufficiently served on the director or authorised representative` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) (a) a copy of the appointment is available; (b) where it was executed by another person, the deed that authorised him or her, verified by statutory declaration.
#ASSERT `s 368(3) what the subsection requires to be available for inspection is available` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368(3) what the subsection requires to be available for inspection is available` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368(3) what the subsection requires to be available for inspection is available` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 368(3) what the subsection requires to be available for inspection is available` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (4) a company not registered under the repealed written laws that had a place of business immediately before and on 29 December 1967.
#ASSERT `s 368(4) subsection (1) applies to the foreign company as if it began on 29 December 1967` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368(4) subsection (1) applies to the foreign company as if it began on 29 December 1967` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 368(4) subsection (1) applies to the foreign company as if it began on 29 December 1967` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 368A`

-- (1) unless the information was previously given in writing.
#ASSERT `s 368A(1) the director must give the foreign company the information it needs to comply with section 372(1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368A(1) the director must give the foreign company the information it needs to comply with section 372(1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) not later than 14 days after the initial appointment: 1 March 2025 + 14 days = 15 March 2025.
#ASSERT `s 368A(1) the director gave the information not later than 14 days after the initial appointment` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368A(1) the director gave the information not later than 14 days after the initial appointment` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the day of the appointment itself and an earlier giving are in time (fork F-P1).
#ASSERT `s 368A(1) the director gave the information not later than 14 days after the initial appointment` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- across the end of February 2025 (28 days): 25 February + 14 days = 11 March.
#ASSERT `s 368A(1) the director gave the information not later than 14 days after the initial appointment` (Date 25 2 2025) (Date 11 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368A(1) the director gave the information not later than 14 days after the initial appointment` (Date 25 2 2025) (Date 12 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2)(a) the same limit for an authorised representative; (2)(b) 14 days after a change in particulars.
#ASSERT `s 368A(2)(a) the authorised representative must give the foreign company the information it needs to comply with section 370(4)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368A(2)(a) the authorised representative must give the foreign company the information it needs to comply with section 370(4)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 368A(2)(a) the authorised representative gave the information not later than 14 days after the initial appointment` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368A(2)(a) the authorised representative gave the information not later than 14 days after the initial appointment` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 368A(2)(b) the authorised representative gave the information not later than 14 days after the change in his or her particulars` (Date 20 6 2025) (Date 4 7 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368A(2)(b) the authorised representative gave the information not later than 14 days after the change in his or her particulars` (Date 20 6 2025) (Date 5 7 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) if requested by the foreign company, for the purpose the subsection names.
#ASSERT `s 368A(3) the director or authorised representative must give the foreign company the information on request` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368A(3) the director or authorised representative must give the foreign company the information on request` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 368A(3) the director or authorised representative must give the foreign company the information on request` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4) not later than 14 days after receipt of the written request.
#ASSERT `s 368A(4) the information was furnished not later than 14 days after receipt of the written request` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 24 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368A(4) the information was furnished not later than 14 days after receipt of the written request` (Date 10 1 2025) (Date 25 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (1) a director: act on day 14 fulfils; day 15 is a breach; nothing by day 15 is a breach; the same day fulfils.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 368A(1) a director must give the foreign company the information within 14 days after the initial appointment` "Ann Lim" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 a director of the foreign company` "Ann Lim" DOES `s 368A give the foreign company the information it needs` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 368A(1) a director must give the foreign company the information within 14 days after the initial appointment` "Ann Lim" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 a director of the foreign company` "Ann Lim" DOES `s 368A give the foreign company the information it needs` AT 15
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 368A(1) a director must give the foreign company the information within 14 days after the initial appointment` "Ann Lim" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 368A(1) a director must give the foreign company the information within 14 days after the initial appointment` "Ann Lim" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 a director of the foreign company` "Ann Lim" DOES `s 368A give the foreign company the information it needs` AT 0
-- (2) an authorised representative.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 368A(2) an authorised representative must give the foreign company the information within 14 days` "Raj Nair" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` "Raj Nair" DOES `s 368A give the foreign company the information it needs` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 368A(2) an authorised representative must give the foreign company the information within 14 days` "Raj Nair" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)
-- (4) a director or authorised representative, on a written request.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 368A(4) the director or authorised representative must furnish the information within 14 days after the written request` (`s 365 a director of the foreign company` "Ann Lim") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 a director of the foreign company` "Ann Lim" DOES `s 368A give the foreign company the information it needs` AT 14
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 368A(4) the director or authorised representative must furnish the information within 14 days after the written request` (`s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` "Raj Nair") AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- (5) the offence: the director or authorised representative who is bound and fails: fine up to $5,000 and a default penalty; the subsection states no term of imprisonment (NOTHING).
#ASSERT (`s 368A(5) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` TRUE TRUE)'s `s 368A(5) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 368A(5) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` TRUE TRUE)'s `s 368A(5) the maximum fine, in dollars` EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT (`s 368A(5) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` TRUE TRUE)'s `s 368A(5) the maximum term of imprisonment, in months` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 368A(5) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` TRUE TRUE)'s `s 368A(5) a default penalty also applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not bound: no offence under the subsection.
#ASSERT (`s 368A(5) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` FALSE TRUE)'s `s 368A(5) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 368A(5) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` FALSE TRUE)'s `s 368A(5) the maximum fine, in dollars` EQUALS NOTHING
-- bound and complied: no offence.
#ASSERT (`s 368A(5) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` TRUE FALSE)'s `s 368A(5) the offence applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a person who is neither a director nor an authorised representative: the subsection does not name them.
#ASSERT (`s 368A(5) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: someone else` TRUE TRUE)'s `s 368A(5) the offence applies` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 368A(5) the offence and its penalty` `s 365 role: an officer of the foreign company` TRUE TRUE)'s `s 368A(5) the offence applies` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 368B`

-- (1)(a) the name and particulars lodged under former s 368(1)(c) stand until a change is notified under s 372(1)(ca).
#ASSERT `s 368B(1)(a) the lodged name and particulars are treated as those of the foreign company's directors` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368B(1)(a) the lodged name and particulars are treated as those of the foreign company's directors` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 368B(1)(a) the lodged name and particulars are treated as those of the foreign company's directors` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(b) the same for agents, treated as authorised representatives.
#ASSERT `s 368B(1)(b) the lodged name and particulars of the agents are treated as those of the foreign company's authorised representatives` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368B(1)(b) the lodged name and particulars of the agents are treated as those of the foreign company's authorised representatives` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) the addresses lodged are treated as residential addresses.
#ASSERT `s 368B(2)(a) the address lodged for a director is treated as the director's residential address` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368B(2)(a) the address lodged for a director is treated as the director's residential address` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 368B(2)(b) the address lodged for an agent is treated as the agent's residential address as authorised representative` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 368B(2)(b) the address lodged for an agent is treated as the agent's residential address as authorised representative` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 369`

#ASSERT `s 369(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 369(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 369(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) within 30 days of the decision: 1 January 2025 + 30 days = 31 January 2025.
#ASSERT `s 369(2) the foreign company may appeal to the Minister` TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 31 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 369(2) the foreign company may appeal to the Minister` TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 369(2) the foreign company may appeal to the Minister` FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 10 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 369(2) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 369(2) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 370`

-- (1) a registered office, open and accessible for not less than 5 hours between 9 a.m. and 5 p.m.
#ASSERT `s 370(1) the registered office meets the subsection on the business day` TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370(1) the registered office meets the subsection on the business day` TRUE 8 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370(1) the registered office meets the subsection on the business day` TRUE 4 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 370(1) the registered office meets the subsection on the business day` FALSE 8 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no deadline in the text: the duty has no breach path; with no event the obligation stays open, and an act at any time fulfils it.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 370(1) the foreign company must have a registered office in Singapore open and accessible to the public` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 370(1) the foreign company must have a registered office in Singapore open and accessible to the public` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 370(1) keep a registered office in Singapore open and accessible to the public` AT 400

-- (2) until the authorised representative ceases in accordance with (5): continues to be, is answerable; personally liable unless the court is satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 370(2)(a) the person continues to be the authorised representative of the foreign company` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370(2)(a) the person continues to be the authorised representative of the foreign company` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 370(2)(b) the person is answerable for the acts, matters and things the foreign company must do under this Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370(2)(b) the person is answerable for the acts, matters and things the foreign company must do under this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 370(2)(c) the person is personally liable to the penalties imposed on the foreign company for a contravention of this Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370(2)(c) the person is personally liable to the penalties imposed on the foreign company for a contravention of this Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 370(2)(c) the person is personally liable to the penalties imposed on the foreign company for a contravention of this Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) the foreign company or its authorised representative may lodge a notice of cessation.
#ASSERT `s 370(3) the person may lodge a notice that the authorised representative has ceased or will cease` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370(3) the person may lodge a notice that the authorised representative has ceased or will cease` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) on the appointment of a new authorised representative, lodge the notice and the consent statement.
#ASSERT `s 370(4) the foreign company has lodged the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370(4) the foreign company has lodged the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 370(4) the foreign company has lodged the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 370(4) the foreign company has lodged the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 370(4) the foreign company must lodge the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 370(4) the foreign company must lodge the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 370(4) lodge the notice and the consent statement for the new authorised representative` AT 3

-- (5) the day the authorised representative ceases. The notice was lodged on 1 March 2025; the 21 days expire on 22 March 2025.
-- Arguments: sole; day the notice was lodged; consent statement for another lodged; the day it was lodged; the notice states a date; that date.
#ASSERT `s 370(5) the day the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 22 3 2025)
-- the consent statement for another representative is lodged earlier, on 10 March: the earlier of the two.
#ASSERT `s 370(5) the day the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2025)
-- lodged later, on 25 March: the 21 days expire first.
#ASSERT `s 370(5) the day the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) TRUE (Date 25 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 22 3 2025)
-- the notice states 30 March, later than the expiration: that date, even though a consent statement was lodged on 10 March.
#ASSERT `s 370(5) the day the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 30 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 3 2025)
#ASSERT `s 370(5) the day the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE (Date 30 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 3 2025)
-- the notice states 20 March, earlier than the expiration: the text gives effect only to a later date, so the 21 days run.
#ASSERT `s 370(5) the day the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 22 3 2025)
-- the date stated is the day the 21 days expire: not later than it, so the same day either way.
#ASSERT `s 370(5) the day the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 22 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 22 3 2025)
-- the sole authorised representative: subsection (6)(b) governs, not (5).
#ASSERT `s 370(5) the day the authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (6)(a) where the notice was lodged by the sole authorised representative the foreign company must appoint another; (b) the day it ceases.
#ASSERT `s 370(6)(a) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370(6)(a) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 370(6)(b) the day the sole authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2025)
#ASSERT `s 370(6)(b) the day the sole authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` TRUE FALSE (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 370(6)(b) the day the sole authorised representative ceases to be an authorised representative` FALSE TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- no deadline in (6)(a): a late appointment still fulfils it.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 370(6)(a) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 370(6)(a) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 370(6)(a) appoint another authorised representative` AT 400

-- (7) within 21 days after the death of the sole authorised representative: 1 March 2025 + 21 days = 22 March 2025.
#ASSERT `s 370(7) the foreign company appointed another authorised representative within 21 days after the death` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 22 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370(7) the foreign company appointed another authorised representative within 21 days after the death` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 23 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 370(7) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative within 21 days after the death of the sole authorised representative` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 370(7) appoint another authorised representative after the death of the sole authorised representative` AT 21
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 370(7) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative within 21 days after the death of the sole authorised representative` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 370(7) appoint another authorised representative after the death of the sole authorised representative` AT 22
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 370(7) the foreign company must appoint another authorised representative within 21 days after the death of the sole authorised representative` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 22)

§ `Section 370A`

-- the commencement date is a supplied fact; the section's own text does not state it.
#ASSERT `s 370A(6) "commencement date" the commencement date` (Date 9 12 2024) EQUALS Date 9 12 2024
-- (1) an alternate address maintained immediately before the commencement date is the contact address until notice of a change is lodged.
#ASSERT `s 370A(1) the alternate address is taken to be the individual's contact address` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370A(1) the alternate address is taken to be the individual's contact address` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 370A(1) the alternate address is taken to be the individual's contact address` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) no alternate address maintained: the residential address, until notice of a change is lodged.
#ASSERT `s 370A(2) the residential address is taken to be the individual's contact address` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370A(2) the residential address is taken to be the individual's contact address` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 370A(2) the residential address is taken to be the individual's contact address` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) the contact address mentioned in (1) or (2) is deemed a particular lodged under s 368(1) for s 372(1)(ca).
#ASSERT `s 370A(3) the contact address is deemed to be a particular lodged with the Registrar under section 368(1) for section 372(1)(ca)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 370A(3) the contact address is deemed to be a particular lodged with the Registrar under section 368(1) for section 372(1)(ca)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) and (5) a notice or information for a director or authorised representative appointed before the commencement date, lodged on or after it.
#ASSERT `s 370A(5) the notice or information must provide the information required under section 368 as in force when it is lodged or given` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
